@*
    One person on the Access screen: who they are, their roles and their tenant, and an Edit that opens their
    editor (docs/architecture/admin-dashboard-review.md, F-13). The row holds nothing being edited: every change is
    made in PersonEditor, which the page owns, and the row reads the list again after it.

    A temporary lockout from failed sign-ins is said in the meta, in the operator's time (LockoutWords): an operator
    asked why somebody cannot sign in otherwise sees an ordinary, enabled person (docs/todo-admin.md §8d item 39).
*@
@inject AdminInterop Interop
@* A stable id per person, so a row can be addressed by who it is rather than by where it sits in a list
   that reorders. *@
<ListRow id="@($"person-{Person.Id.Value}")" class="a-listrow--roomy a-listrow--inline a-listrow--center">
    <span class="a-grow a-grow--wide">
        <span class="a-name">@Person.Email</span>
        <span class="a-meta">
            @(Person.RoleNames.Count == 0 ? "no roles" : string.Join(", ", Person.RoleNames)) ·
            @(Person.Tenant is { } tenant ? $"tenant {tenant.Value}" : "no tenant")
            @if (Person.IsDisabled)
            {
                <text> · disabled</text>
            }
            @if (LockoutWords.Of(Person, Interop.UtcOffset) is { } locked)
            {
                <text> · </text><span data-testid="person-locked">@locked</span>
            }
        </span>
    </span>

    <AlvoButton Tone="AlvoButton.ButtonTone.Ghost" Small="true" id="@($"change-{Person.Id.Value}")"
                aria-label="@($"Edit {Person.Email}")" OnClick="_ => OnOpen.InvokeAsync()">Edit</AlvoButton>
</ListRow>

@code {
    /// <summary>The person this row is about.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public AlvoUser Person { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Raised by Edit, to open the person's editor.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnOpen { get; set; }
}
